{"sha":"bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144","node_id":"C_kwDOR-4UedoAKGJhYjA4NDQ0M2YxNGU2YWIzYmE3NmY4ZThlM2Y3MjFhZDJlNTYxNDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sean Phan","email":"seanphan@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-04-10T08:54:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"Sean Phan","email":"seanphan@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-04-10T08:54:13Z"},"message":"Add reproduction handoff notes\n\nContext for continuing megakernel benchmark reproduction on\nnative Windows RTX 3090. Documents known issues (transformers\ncompat, cooperative grid sync), build steps, and WSL baseline\nresults.","tree":{"sha":"1d7bfa4a264f7610e3b4fd93a05d3b2c534ce5a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PixelML/luce-megakernel/git/trees/1d7bfa4a264f7610e3b4fd93a05d3b2c534ce5a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PixelML/luce-megakernel/git/commits/bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PixelML/luce-megakernel/commits/bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144","html_url":"https://github.com/PixelML/luce-megakernel/commit/bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PixelML/luce-megakernel/commits/bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144/comments","author":{"login":"seanphan","id":5804000,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MDQwMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5804000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan","html_url":"https://github.com/seanphan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"seanphan","id":5804000,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MDQwMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5804000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan","html_url":"https://github.com/seanphan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanphan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aa16696280b483c31d35c89382f225f19a63bdc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PixelML/luce-megakernel/commits/aa16696280b483c31d35c89382f225f19a63bdc7","html_url":"https://github.com/PixelML/luce-megakernel/commit/aa16696280b483c31d35c89382f225f19a63bdc7"}],"stats":{"total":108,"additions":108,"deletions":0},"files":[{"sha":"ff724c69ba77b3e93df5b786898124837c79e05a","filename":"HANDOFF.md","status":"added","additions":108,"deletions":0,"changes":108,"blob_url":"https://github.com/PixelML/luce-megakernel/blob/bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144/HANDOFF.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/PixelML/luce-megakernel/raw/bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144/HANDOFF.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PixelML/luce-megakernel/contents/HANDOFF.md?ref=bab084443f14e6ab3ba76f8e8e3f721ad2e56144","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n+# Megakernel Reproduction Handoff\n+\n+## Goal\n+Reproduce the luce-megakernel benchmark (Qwen3.5-0.8B fused CUDA kernel) on this RTX 3090 machine natively on Windows. Compare results to the reported 413 tok/s decode, 37,800 tok/s prefill.\n+\n+## Repo\n+- **Source**: `https://github.com/PixelML/luce-megakernel` (forked from Luce-Org)\n+- **Clone location on this machine**: `C:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\WIP\\luce-megakernel-win`\n+- Original: `https://github.com/Luce-Org/luce-megakernel`\n+\n+## What's Already Done on This Machine\n+1. **CUDA 12.3** installed (`nvcc` in PATH)\n+2. **MSVC Build Tools 2022** at `C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\2022\\BuildTools`\n+   - vcvarsall: `\"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\2022\\BuildTools\\VC\\Auxiliary\\Build\\vcvarsall.bat\" amd64`\n+3. **Python 3.9** at `C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\Shared\\Python39_64`\n+4. **Venv** at `C:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\WIP\\luce-megakernel\\.winvenv` with:\n+   - PyTorch 2.5.1+cu121\n+   - transformers (from git, v4.57.6)\n+   - accelerate\n+   - safetensors\n+5. The repo was cloned to `luce-megakernel-win` but build was NOT completed there yet.\n+\n+## Steps to Build & Run\n+\n+```cmd\n+:: 1. Activate MSVC\n+call \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\2022\\BuildTools\\VC\\Auxiliary\\Build\\vcvarsall.bat\" amd64\n+\n+:: 2. Activate venv (reuse existing one or create new)\n+C:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\WIP\\luce-megakernel\\.winvenv\\Scripts\\activate.bat\n+\n+:: 3. Set required env var\n+set DISTUTILS_USE_SDK=1\n+\n+:: 4. cd to repo\n+cd C:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\WIP\\luce-megakernel-win\n+\n+:: 5. Build CUDA extension\n+python setup.py build_ext --inplace\n+\n+:: 6. Run benchmark\n+python bench_pp_tg.py\n+```\n+\n+## Known Issues & Fixes Needed\n+\n+### 1. transformers doesn't recognize `qwen3_5` model type\n+The Qwen3.5-0.8B model uses `model_type: \"qwen3_5\"` which isn't in any released transformers version yet. \n+\n+**Fix**: Add this to the TOP of `model.py` (after `import torch`):\n+```python\n+try:\n+    from transformers.models.auto.configuration_auto import CONFIG_MAPPING\n+    if \"qwen3_5\" not in CONFIG_MAPPING:\n+        CONFIG_MAPPING.register(\"qwen3_5\", CONFIG_MAPPING[\"qwen3_next\"])\n+except Exception:\n+    pass\n+```\n+BUT this alias causes a crash in `GenerationConfig.from_model_config` because the config structures differ.\n+\n+**Better fix**: Bypass AutoModelForCausalLM entirely. Replace the `load_weights()` function body to load safetensors directly:\n+```python\n+from safetensors.torch import load_file\n+import glob, os\n+\n+tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n+cache_dir = os.path.expanduser(\"~/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--\" + model_name.replace(\"/\", \"--\"))\n+snap = os.path.join(cache_dir, \"snapshots\", os.listdir(os.path.join(cache_dir, \"snapshots\"))[0])\n+raw = {}\n+for sf in glob.glob(os.path.join(snap, \"*.safetensors\")):\n+    raw.update(load_file(sf, device=\"cuda\"))\n+# Safetensors keys have \"model.language_model.\" prefix, model.py expects \"model.\"\n+state = {k.replace(\"model.language_model.\", \"model.\"): v.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous() for k, v in raw.items()}\n+del raw\n+```\n+Delete the `del model` line too since there's no model object.\n+\n+### 2. Decode kernel deadlocks (WSL only, may not affect native Windows)\n+On WSL2, the decode kernel's cooperative grid sync deadlocked because `<<<>>>` launch doesn't guarantee all 82 blocks run simultaneously. Fixed by using `cudaLaunchCooperativeKernel` in `kernel.cu`. \n+\n+On native Windows this MAY work without the fix since the CUDA driver is native (not virtualized). Try without the fix first. If decode hangs, apply the cooperative launch patch from the WSL repo at `C:\\Users\\ADMIN\\Desktop\\WIP\\luce-megakernel\\kernel.cu`.\n+\n+### 3. WSL Results (for comparison)\n+With cooperative launch fix on WSL2:\n+- pp302: 2,338 tok/s  \n+- tg128: 62.2 tok/s\n+- Correctness: FAIL (prefill+decode diverged from reference)\n+\n+These are much worse than reported (37,800 / 413). WSL GPU-PV overhead + NTFS filesystem explain most of it.\n+\n+## Architecture Summary\n+- `kernel.cu` (960 lines): Single persistent CUDA kernel for decode. All 24 layers (18 DeltaNet + 6 Full Attention) in one dispatch. 82 blocks x 512 threads. Uses cooperative grid sync between layers.\n+- `prefill.cu` (462 lines): Prefill uses cuBLAS bf16 GEMM + standalone kernels.\n+- `model.py`: Weight loading from HuggingFace, packs layer pointers into device blob.\n+- `bench_pp_tg.py`: Correctness test + pp512/tg128 benchmarks.\n+- `setup.py`: Build config targeting sm_86 (RTX 3090).\n+\n+## Model\n+- Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B (bf16, ~1.5GB VRAM)\n+- 24 layers: 18 DeltaNet (linear attention with recurrence) + 6 Full Attention\n+- Layer pattern: [DN,DN,DN,FA, DN,DN,DN,FA, ...] x6\n+\n+## Expected Results (from repo README)\n+| Method | pp512 (tok/s) | tg128 (tok/s) |\n+|--------|:---:|:---:|\n+| Megakernel | 37,800 | 413 |\n+| llama.cpp BF16 | 11,247 | 267 |\n+| PyTorch HF | 7,578 | 108 |"}]}